# A CANDIDATE: A CANARY REFUSED FOR MEMORY IS NOT A CANARY THAT FAILED (the
# node, 2026-11-25 09:40:55Z, live d531d5d804f1: one context of an embedding
# model discarded as "context canary failed" in the second the card filled at
# a worker's start; Louise set the run's statements aside and gated the
# collection again, forty minutes - docs/notes/parking-step-2.md 6b).
# engine-stream.series (792f050e318e), line for line, then:
#   0028  a context canary whose graph the device refuses for memory. At a
#         request it is a context that cannot be created ("the context cannot
#         be created now ... try again later", counted nowhere as a canary
#         that failed); at the load it fails the load, where the model was
#         served UNCHECKED. A canary that was computed and differs is what it
#         was. No new error type: that stays 0023's.
#   SERIES_FILE=deploy/localai/patches/staged/engine-canary.series \
#     sh deploy/localai/llama-cpp/build.sh sycl_f16 <out dir>      # the live INTEL_STACK
# ONE BUILD, ONE GATING for the paging default (0021), the language tag (0022),
# the stream (0025) and this: it stands in 792f050e318e's place if that one is
# not gated yet. engine-park.series does NOT list 0028 and must not: 0023
# carries the same fix in its own form, on the same lines.
# Its row, on a COPY of an encoder with context on demand whose env has
# GGML_SYCL_GRAPH_REFUSE=2 and GGML_SYCL_GRAPH_REFUSE_ARM=<file> (0026): once
# its context is gone, create the file and send one request - refused with
# "the context cannot be created now", no context counted as discarded - then
# remove the file: the next request is served.
base dd5780aa904d132c784867d37fc713df8d984c8a
